# Purposeful code (mandatory)

Vaikuntham code exists to ship hostel operations. If a change does not serve a current user need, Linear story, or proven bug, do not write it.

## Before writing

1. Name the **user-facing purpose** (one sentence).
2. Name the **Linear issue** (e.g. CB-127) or explicit user request.
3. Prefer extending an existing module over a new abstraction.

## Do not add

- Unused helpers, types, hooks, or components “for later”
- Speculative config, feature flags, or empty folders
- Comments that restate the code; only explain non-obvious *why*
- Extra dependencies when stdlib / existing libs suffice
- Duplicate UI patterns when `components/ui/*` already covers it
- Logging of PII; audit via `writeAuditLog` for sensitive writes only

## When changing code

- Delete dead code in the same change when you replace it
- Keep Server Actions thin: authz → validate (Zod) → transaction → audit
- Money: integer paise only; tenancy: always scope by `hostelId`
- One primary CTA per page header; no decorative cards in hero-style chrome

## PR / agent checklist

- [ ] Purpose stated (comment in PR or commit body)
- [ ] Linked to a story or user ask
- [ ] No files added without a caller
- [ ] No new abstraction used in fewer than two places (wait for the second use)
